  "articleBody": "Adding a room to your home is a fantastic way to gain space, but navigating the permit process for your addition framing can feel like a maze. It’s a super important step because inspections for things like rough framing need to pass before insulation or drywall goes in. The timing for permits and inspections can vary widely depending on where you live, so don't be surprised if it takes a few weeks or even months for approvals. A common mistake is underestimating this lead time, which can really push back your project's start date. Your first step should always be finalizing your scope and getting those drawings ready for submission. You'll need to secure all the necessary permits before any significant work begins. It’s also crucial to procure your lumber and other materials well in advance, as delays in sourcing can stall your project. Remember, if your addition changes the structure or involves new load-bearing walls, having an experienced framing contractor and design professionals on board is key. They can help ensure your plans are permit-ready and that everything is built to code, saving you headaches and potential rework down the line. If you're feeling overwhelmed, give us a call to discuss your project!",
